{#-
This Template generates IIIF 3.0 API Manifest capable of handling Digital Objects and Creative Works Series using a Drupal Views
using the Solr Indexed RAW JSON field to avoid pre-rendering canvases. It is more efficient/less memory/less CPU.
Right now only Renders as:image based Children Canvases, but can be extended to deal with all media

Last updated Nov 19 2026 by Diego Pino for 2.2.0. 
     - Ensures Array for requiredStatement
     - Improves logic on ispartof to accumuluate both ispartof and ismemberof with better validation
     - requiredStatement label should be Rights not Attribution 
     - rename description to summary
     - switch to the more common creator_lod instead of edm_agent
     - use ";" notation on page number for PDF based thumbnails 
     - Fixes extra comma (legacy based on loop.last) when Child ADO has multiple images
     - Adds Text based Annotations to the Top processing
     
Previously updated 05/12/2025 for 1.6.0. IIIF Presentation API 3 Series Manifest Unified 
- Uses a single Search API Views, paged, bringing children up to two level downs. -
Sorts by more far away Sequence id, then lowering to its own.
Also adds the "," before instead at the end. That way we always know IF we will end outputting. I should have known this before!
Previously updated 31/05/2024 for 1.4.0 & Scrapbook. Content Search API matching the exposed manifest iiifmanifest3cws_scrapbook
Previously updated 31/05/2024 for 1.4.0 & Scrapbook. 3 levels down of canvases
Previously updated 31/11/2023 for 1.3.0. Fixes Video/Audio Urls when attached directly to a top object

Previously Updated 31/10/2023 for 1.3.0 

- Includes top level objects too now.
Structures passed from Archipelago are
- node
  The full Node entity
- data
  The Full JSON Structure converted in an Array
- iiif_server
  The publicly available IIIF Server (Global Setting)​ 
Since JSON was decoded into the 'data' values are valid PHP but could not
be valid JSON when outputting. So We use data.description|json_encode|raw
Without Double quotes.
-#}
{%- set structureCanvasIds = [] %}
{# with 150 being Cantaloupe's setup PDF rastering resolution and 72 what PDFINFO produces by default #} 
{%- set pdf_resolution = (150/72) %} 
{%- set baseurl =  url('<front>')|render -%} 
{%- set Webserverurl =  baseurl -%} 
{%- set IIIFserverurl = iiif_server ? iiif_server ~ '/': Webserverurl -%} 
{%- set currenturl = url('<current>')|render -%} 
{%- set parentcollectionurl = '' -%}
{%- set parentnodeurl = '' %}
{%- set nodeid = node.id|default(1) %}
{%- set max_thumb_width = 240 -%}
{# Defines a limit of how many Children Nodes (View Pages) it will be allowed to get via a Drupal View) #}
{%- set max_views_pages = 500 -%}
{%- set itemCount = 0 -%}
{%- if node.id -%}
	{# this is needed to the View Argument can conform to the format even when no node exists when saving the template #}
    {% set nodeid = node.id %}
    {% set nodeurl = url('entity.node.canonical', {'node': node.id}, {'absolute': true}) %}
{% else %}
    {% set nodeid = 1 %} 
    {% set nodeurl = currenturl %}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if attribute(data, 'ismemberof') %} 
    {%- if attribute(data, 'ismemberof') is iterable -%} 
	    {%- for collection in attribute(data, 'ismemberof') -%} 
		   {%- set parentcollectionurl = url('entity.node.canonical', {'node': collection}, {'absolute': true}) -%} 
	    {%- endfor -%} 
	{%- else -%} 
		{%- set parentcollectionurl = url('entity.node.canonical', {'node': attribute(data, 'ismemberof')}, {'absolute': true}) -%} 
    {%- endif -%} 
{%- endif -%} 
{%- if attribute(data, 'ispartof') -%} 
    {%- if attribute(data, 'ispartof') is iterable -%} 
	{%- for child in attribute(data, 'ispartof') -%} 
		{%- set parentnodeurl = url('entity.node.canonical', {'node': child}, {'absolute': true}) -%} 
	{%- endfor -%} 
	{%- else -%} 
		{%- set parentnodeurl = url('entity.node.canonical', {'node': attribute(data, 'ispartof')}, {'absolute': true}) -%} 
   {%- endif -%} 
{%- endif -%} 
